{"game": "roboquest", "language": "english", "appid": 692890, "month": "2025-10", "window": 3, "start_date": 1760572800, "end_date": 1761263999, "month_true_total": 140, "quota": 5, "returned": 5, "pulled_at": "2026-10-03 01:55:53 UTC", "reviews": [{"recommendationid": "207408865", "author": {"steamid": "76561198082440113", "personaname": "D-Glad", "persona_status": "in-game", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198082440113/", "num_games_owned": 275, "num_reviews": 40, "playtime_forever": 231, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 231, "last_played": 1761245881, "avatar": "511c40852dbdd91dedd9d8f3fd8d7eb738c0fc78"}, "language": "english", "review": "Fun game, mostly. A roguelike FPS with a healthy assortment of random weapons to find, what's not to like? Well, how about performance issues? After a couple hours of playing, I was getting frame drops and stuttering that eventually made it impossible for me to actually play the game. I would have loved to just save and quit, but you can't save a run in the middle. I've read that you can save at certain points/after bosses (maybe?) but I never saw the option. I wound up just quitting out of frustration.\r\nI have some issues with the gameplay, but it's mostly good. It's a shame, because if the performance was better or if I could just pause a run to try to fix it, I would be delighted to praise this game, but the problems are just way too distracting.", "timestamp_created": 1761246643, "timestamp_updated": 1761246643, "voted_up": false, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.454545468091964722", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1597939791", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "207373896", "author": {"steamid": "76561198031040638", "personaname": "tstaylor26", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamc